{
  "reason": "Ceilings are the Ergo-only bytes (fixture minus the Go hello control, default and stripped builds) measured on linux/amd64 with go1.27.0, plus 2 %, rounded up; Go package ceilings likewise. BS0 set them at main f6802de7; BS1 (runtime/v1 leaves), BS2 (core without fmt and reflect), BS3 (no time type in the task's type graph), BS5 (frontend reachability: unused equals hello) and BS6 (relative paths and compact call tables) lowered them; BS7 (machine graphs as static data, no init-time registration) added pairing, an actor program, with its registry facts; BS8 (the stack landed on batch 17, with http, rpc, redacted, exec start and the host walk in leaves) raised every fixture's ceiling to its measured value plus 2 % for the batch-17 code the stack had not seen: the core's json.go and moves.go initializers and ergoStack's new frames (hello +4 KB stripped), std flag's parser (kvstore main +64 KB) and the core's JSON text (deploys, pairing); it narrowed the registry facts to the start-up registration (RegisterMachine, RegisteredGraph, main.init.N), since a generic flat union's ErgoVariant reads VariantOf lazily on the trace path. A unit that shrinks a fixture lowers its ceilings to its measured value plus 2 %; a unit that grows one past a ceiling raises it only with the reason in its request. Forbid lists facts: patterns of linked symbol names that must stay absent. SIZE-HELLO added packages to hello, pure and unused: the Go packages whose code each may link (runtime/debug stands for the runtime's own setGCPercent, setMemoryLimit and setPanicOnFault, which the runtime defines under that name); runtime/metrics is among them for PACE1's goal (its live heap and scan roots), the only package PACE1 adds. SIZE-HELLO also put a ledger beside each ceiling: base is the ceilings before the first recorded raise, and each raise names its unit, the two measured commits, its owners with their symbol bytes (go tool nm -size) and largest symbols, and the Go packages it adds; Checked refuses a ceiling above base plus its raises, so the next raise names its bytes too. Make one with `go run ./internal/sizes/cmd/sizes -keep DIR` at both commits and diff the binaries (SIZE-HELLO round-2 request).",
